.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt NQSEAL2 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqseal2 ,
.Nm nqcapid
.Nd seal a format 2 capsule, and a capsule's id
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Bd -literal
typedef struct {
  uint8_t id[32];
  const char *name;
} nqcin;
.Ed
.Pp
.Ft int
.Fo nqseal2
.Fa "const char *dir" "nqsalg alg"
.Fa "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen"
.Fa "const char *meta"
.Fa "const nqcin *in" "size_t nin"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fn nqcapid "const char *dir" "uint8_t id[32]"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqseal2
is
.Xr nqseal 3
in format 2
.Pq Ql noqtis-capsule-2 , Ql noqtis-seal-2 , Xr noqtis-capsule 5 :
the manifest also carries a Merkle tree over its file entries, and the
seal signs the manifest's head, which holds the tree's root and size but
not the list of files.
.Xr nqprove 3
can then show single files without the others.
.Pp
.Fa in Ns Bq 0..nin
are the capsules this one was made from, at most 1024, recorded in the
manifest's
.Ql inputs :
each
.Fa id
is an input's id from
.Fn nqcapid ,
and each
.Fa name
1 to 255 bytes of UTF-8 with no control character.
.Fa in
may be
.Dv NULL
when
.Fa nin
is 0.
.Xr nqchkx 3
follows these records with its
.Fa lin
folders.
.Pp
.Fn nqcapid
stores in
.Fa id
the id of the capsule in
.Fa dir :
the SHA-256 of the bytes its seal signs
.Pq Ql manifest_sha256 No of a format 1 seal, Ql head_sha256 No of a format 2 one ,
read from
.Pa noqtis.sig .
Nothing else is checked: check the capsule
.Pq Xr nqchk 3
before relying on it.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn nqseal2
returns what
.Xr nqseal 3
returns, and
.Er NQEARG
for an input name that is empty, too long or has a control character, and
.Er NQELIM
for more than 1024 inputs.
.Fn nqcapid
returns
.Dv NQOK ,
.Er NQEIO
when the seal cannot be read,
.Er NQEDEC
when it is not a seal of either format, or
.Er NQEARG .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 ,
.Xr nqchkx 3 ,
.Xr nqprove 3 ,
.Xr nqseal 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
